{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792612145,"nonce":"bNyIK6CI+1kaLJs1CAYPtt8q9CA=","title":"Instantiate call signatures during editor validation","message":"RayDE src/rayde/term/Profiles.hx is valid Haxe but reports seven typing diagnostics: expected T found Bool at Map\u003cString, Bool\u003e.set, Null\u003cString\u003e/String comparisons and arguments, and optional local-function calls presented as identical expected/found signatures.\n\nThe post-lowering checker reads raw method declarations and drops their receiver and call type arguments, rather than using the generic bindings already established by lowering. Its arity check also requires every optional local argument, whose flags were lost when constructing the function type. Null\u003cString\u003e is treated as a distinct non-nullable value despite String already being a nullable reference type in Haxe.\n\nShare the existing lowering substitution routines with call validation. Receiver bindings must take precedence over argument-derived bindings so invalid Map\u003cString, Bool\u003e.set(key, 123) remains an error. Preserve optional function labels; validate all supplied arguments and required arity. Keep nullable value-type checks while recognizing reference nullability and symmetric equality compatibility. Dynamic calls are legal, but calling a concrete number remains an error.\n\nRegression coverage includes the Profiles pattern, generic identity and inherited generic methods, wrong map values, missing required arguments, and non-callable values. Validation is underway.","files":null}]}